      "task_id": "86d12areh",
      "suggestion_type": "analysis",
      "suggestion_text": "{\"score\":1,\"suggestion\":\"Split this task and add comprehensive acceptance criteria, detailed user stories, and estimations.\",\"reasoning\":\"The title 'Redesign Complete UI' is far too broad and vague. The empty description compounds the problem. Without a more precise scope, acceptance criteria, and smaller, more manageable sub-tasks, the team cannot effectively plan, estimate, or execute this work. 'Complete UI' is extremely ambiguous - what UI elements are included? What constitutes a redesign (visual refresh, architectural changes, functionality updates)? This single item represents a large, undefined effort. The lack of a description makes it impossible to understand the intent or the value it delivers.\"}",
      "status": "pending",
      "created_at": "2025-11-26T08:53:34.156848"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "task_id": "86d132m8z",
      "suggestion_type": "analysis",
      "suggestion_text": "{\"score\":8,\"suggestion\":\"Add acceptance criteria\",\"reasoning\":\"The backlog item is generally well-written with a clear title, description, steps to reproduce, expected and actual results, severity, and type. However, explicitly stating acceptance criteria would make the item even clearer and easier to test. Examples of acceptance criteria include: 'The entire dropdown list is visible for all rows, even when the dropdown is located at the bottom of the scrollable container' or 'When the dropdown list would be cut off at the bottom, it automatically expands upwards so all options are visible'.\"}",
      "status": "pending",
